Hi Zhong Miao,

Thank you for bringing this matter to our attention and for the details
provided regarding the suspected origin hijacking.
We understand your concern regarding the announcement of APNIC-assigned
address space by AS202734.

APNIC (like AfriNIC, ARIN, LACNIC, and RIPE NCC) is a Regional
Internet Registry (RIR) with a narrow mandate relating to technical
and operational issues.

The primary role of the RIRs is to register IP addresses and other
resources to the organizations using them and to provide a public
database where those registrations can be viewed. The RIRs have not
been given any role to enforce standards of behaviour in relation to
what is done with those resources. The RIRs simply have no legal
authority to do that.

Furthermore, the RIRs do not provide connectivity to users of
Internet resources and therefore have no way to disconnect any users.

To help mitigate the issue, we recommend you to contact the originating
network (AS202734) via:

  =E2=80=A2 WHOIS contact details
  =E2=80=A2 Abuse or NOC email addresses

Kind regards,
Lu
